From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Smith <scott@newtrostudios.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:37:09 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0304): host releases held keys and buttons when a
 connection ends

DEF-7, AC-41. Upstream releases almost nothing when a connection ends:
release_pressed_modifiers (Drop for Connection) covers a set that is
nearly always empty, held keys are force-released only after six
minutes or at process exit, and mouse buttons never. A drop mid-drag or
with a key held left it stuck on the host.

The connection's input thread now tracks every key and button it
injects (HeldInput) and, when the connection's input channel closes,
injects the matching up events through the same path as the downs (the
main-thread queue on macOS, the portable service on Windows when it
runs), buttons first so a drag ends where it is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
